# >>> LV-LINK-PRELOAD (managed by apply_link_preload_headers.py)
# 🔴 HAND-MAINTAINED SINCE 2026-08-10 — the generator writes ONE line per site
# and this hero is art-directed: a landscape flat-lay on desktop, a portrait
# one on phones (src/components/Hero.tsx explains why). Preloading the old
# single hero-main.jpg would now fetch 332 kB that the page never renders,
# because <picture> resolves to AVIF. The preload matters more here than on a
# server-rendered site: #root ships empty, so without these the hero is not
# even discovered until the bundle has parsed. If the generator is re-run for
# this site, restore this block by hand.
/
  Link: </images/hero-main.avif>; rel=preload; as=image; type=image/avif; media="(min-width: 768px)"; fetchpriority=high
  Link: </images/hero-main-portrait.avif>; rel=preload; as=image; type=image/avif; media="(max-width: 767px)"; fetchpriority=high

/index.html
  Link: </images/hero-main.avif>; rel=preload; as=image; type=image/avif; media="(min-width: 768px)"; fetchpriority=high
  Link: </images/hero-main-portrait.avif>; rel=preload; as=image; type=image/avif; media="(max-width: 767px)"; fetchpriority=high
